  "raw": {
    "https://cbu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204168": {
      "title": "Dean of the McEniry School of Business, Education, and Humanities",
      "description": "Christian Brothers University\nJob Posting: Dean of the McEniry School of Business, Education, and Humanities Christian Brothers University \n\tJob Posting: Dean of the McEniry School of Business, Education, and Humanities Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Dean of the McEniry School of Business, Education, and Humanities Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Business, Education, and Humanities Locations: Memphis, TN Posted: Aug 26, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position ID: 204168 Share About Christian Brothers University: CBU is committed to creating and maintaining a rigorous and enriching learning experience for our students by providing them the best instruction and support by a superior faculty and staff. CBU encourages opportunities to celebrate diversity in an environment that prepares our students to be global citizens. CBU is an attractive and safe campus environment, and it is quite possibly one of the friendliest campuses anywhere. If you would like to contribute to these hallmarks of a CBU education, please consider applying for our faculty or staff vacancies through these current employment opportunities. Applicants are encouraged to review the Dean of the McEniry School of Business, Education, and Humanities Prospectus linked here for comprehensive search details on the position, institutional context, leadership expectations, and application requirements. Job Description: Position Summary The Dean of the McEniry School of Business, Education, and Humanities reports to the Vice President for Academic Affairs and is the academic officer charged with supervision overall departments and disciplines of the school, including overall responsibility for the curriculum and academic quality. As an academic officer, the Dean assumes a university-wide perspective and a strategic role in communication with the university's constituents including parents, perspective students, potential donors, industry, government, professional societies, and alumni. Responsibilities: Create a vision and strategic plan for the School and develop methods to ensure progression towards both short-term and long-range goals. Coordinate the academic programs relative to university core requirements, requirements for majors within the School, and accreditation; Recruit, supervise, develop, and evaluate the school's faculty and staff; Coordinate and supervise the activities of the Chairs and Program Directors, serving as their primary evaluator; Supervise the school's budget and facilities, and advise the VPAA on annual and long- range budgeting; In consultation with the CBU Office of Advancement, play an active role in university and school fundraising; Provide administrative support for enrollment management and retention initiatives; Maintain a high public profile, interacting with local, regional, and national businesses, educational institutions, and organizations to leverage strategic partnerships, initiatives, collaborations, and internships; Promote innovation and entrepreneurism among faculty to advance new programs and opportunities for our students and provide new revenue streams into the School of Business; Exercise compassionate and Lasallian-inspired leadership while building upon the University's commitment to foster academic excellence and prepare students from all faiths and backgrounds for careers and lives of faith, service, and community Display active support for the Universities mission. Duties as assigned by the Vice President. Requirements: Doctorate degree in the field of Business from a regionally accredited institution and four (4) years administrative experience at the level of dean, department chair, director of a graduate program, or higher. A proven record of scholarship, professional development, and excellence in teaching. Ability to balance and support the diverse needs of students in undergraduate and graduate programs. Preferred Experience: Record of successful fundraising Practical understanding of strategic planning Familiarity with AACSB or ACBSP accreditation processes Experience working, consulting, or record of other professional interactions within the business community. Experience in working collaboratively with Education and Humanities programs. Additional Information: Christian Brothers University is a Catholic university in the student-centered tradition of the De La Salle Christian Brothers. CBU fosters academic excellence in a range of programs to prepare students from all faiths and backgrounds for careers and lives informed by the Lasallian values of faith, service, and community. Christian Brothers University offers a comprehensive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability insurance, flexible spending, 403(b), and both undergraduate and graduate tuition waiver plans. CBU also offers tuition waivers for dependents of employees and participates in the Tuition Exchange Program, a reciprocal scholarship exchange program for family members of full-time faculty and staff. Christian Brothers University offers equal employment opportunity to all applicants for employment, regardless of sex, age, race, color, religion, sexual orientation, national and ethnic origin or disability. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Christian Brothers University 650 East Parkway South, Memphis Tennessee 38104"
    },
    "https://cbu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=198432": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Health Informatics and Data Systems",
      "description": "Christian Brothers University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor - Health Informatics and Data Systems Christian Brothers University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor - Health Informatics and Data Systems Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor - Health Informatics and Data Systems Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Memphis, TN Posted: Mar 24, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 198432 Share About Christian Brothers University: CBU is committed to creating and maintaining a rigorous and enriching learning experience for our students by providing them the best instruction and support by a superior faculty and staff. CBU encourages opportunities to celebrate diversity in an environment that prepares our students to be global citizens. CBU is an attractive and safe campus environment, and it is quite possibly one of the friendliest campuses anywhere. If you would like to contribute to these hallmarks of a CBU education, please consider applying for our faculty or staff vacancies through these current employment opportunities. Job Description: The School of Sciences is seeking a passionate and experienced adjunct faculty member to join our School of Sciences community. The ideal candidate will be responsible for facilitating learning in the Healthcare Informatics and Data Systems didactic setting. Candidates will demonstrate excellence in teaching through innovative evidence-based practice. This role is a wonderful opportunity for a dedicated educator to shape the future of the healthcare workforce with compassionate, skilled, and knowledgeable healthcare professionals. The faculty member will prepare future healthcare professionals to effectively utilize electronic health records, clinical decision support tools, and health data analytics to improve patient outcomes, healthcare quality, and operational efficiency. Key Responsibilities: Facilitate learning in the classroom Facilitate learner development and socialization Utilize assessment and evaluation strategies Participate in course development Function as a change agent and leader Pursue continuous quality improvement Provide academic student support Function cohesively within the educational environment. Exhibit Lasallian principles in the academic community . Requirements: Required Qualifications: Master's degree in Healthcare Informatics, Health Information Management, Health Data Analytics, Health Science, Nursing, Public Health, or a related field. Experience with electronic health records (EHRs), healthcare data systems, or clinical informatics tools. Teaching experience in higher education or professional training related to healthcare or health informatics. Knowledge of healthcare data privacy and regulatory standards (e.g., Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act). Demonstrated ability to integrate healthcare technology into teaching and learning environments. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Healthcare Informatics, Health Science, Nursing, Public Health, or related discipline. Professional certification in health informatics or health information management (e.g., RHIA, CHDA, CPHIMS). Experience with healthcare analytics platforms, population health data systems, or clinical quality improvement data. Experience teaching online or hybrid courses using learning management systems Additional Information: Christian Brothers University is a Catholic university in the student-centered tradition of the De La Salle Christian Brothers. CBU fosters academic excellence in a range of programs to prepare students from all faiths and backgrounds for careers and lives informed by the Lasallian values of faith, service, and community. Christian Brothers University offers a comprehensive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability insurance, flexible spending, retirement pension plan, 403(b), and both undergraduate and graduate tuition waiver plans. CBU also offers tuition waivers for dependents of employees and participates in the Tuition Exchange Program, a reciprocal scholarship exchange program for family members of full-time faculty and staff. Christian Brothers University offers equal employment opportunity to all applicants for employment, regardless of sex, age, race, color, religion, sexual orientation, national and ethnic origin or disability. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Christian Brothers University 650 East Parkway South, Memphis Tennessee 38104"
    },
    "https://cbu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=196384": {
      "title": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor",
      "description": "Christian Brothers University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Clinical Instructor Christian Brothers University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Clinical Instructor Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Clinical Instructor Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Sciences Locations: Memphis, TN Posted: Jan 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Ref. No.: 142816 Position ID: 196384 Share About Christian Brothers University: CBU is committed to creating and maintaining a rigorous and enriching learning experience for our students by providing them the best instruction and support by a superior faculty and staff. CBU encourages opportunities to celebrate diversity in an environment that prepares our students to be global citizens. CBU is an attractive and safe campus environment, and it is quite possibly one of the friendliest campuses anywhere. If you would like to contribute to these hallmarks of a CBU education, please consider applying for our faculty or staff vacancies through these current employment opportunities. Job Description: We are seeking a dedicated and experienced part-time nursing clinical instructor to join our team. This role involves hands-on instruction and supervision to nursing students in the clinical settings, helping them bridge the gap between theoretical knowledge and practical application. The ideal candidate will be a skilled nursing professional with a passion for teaching, mentorship, and fostering the next generation of healthcare providers. THIS POSTING IS NOT A GUARANTEE OF AN OPEN POSITION. Applications for part-time faculty positions are accepted continuously and reviewed by the Director of Nursing and Dean of Sciences when openings become available. Future teaching assignments are made on a semester-by-semester basis, which may include either Fall or Spring. Key Responsibilities: Proactively create an inclusive learning environment. Utilize evidence-based practice and adult learning principles to instruct students in the clinical/laboratory/simulation settings. Understand the objectives of the assigned course, and be familiar with the overall curriculum of the pre-licensure program. Collaborate with preceptors, nurses, clinical managers, staff nurses, and other representatives of the assigned clinical site to plan students' clinical experience. Guide students in delivering safe, quality patient care Mentor the students' development of clinical decision-making and clinical judgment skills, competency in the execution of clinical skills, and effective communication with patients, families, and other members of the health care team Evaluate students' clinical practice and provide feedback on the accomplishments of clinical objectives. Communicate student concerns on time to the course faculty Facilitate learning in the health care environment Participate in all mandatory trainings and/or meetings required before and during the semester, including site-specific orientation Demonstrate effective interpersonal communication and collaborative interprofessional  relationships Apply clinical expertise in the health care environment Facilitate learner development and socialization. Implement practical clinical assessment and evaluation strategies Works under the administrative direction of the Director of Nursing. Requirements: BSN required. Current or eligible for an active, unencumbered Tennessee registered nursing license or multistate licensure privilege to practice as a registered nurse in Tennessee. BLS/ACLS certification as required by the clinical agencies Vaccinations as required by clinical agencies Strong communication and organizational skills Collaborate effectively with stakeholders Three or more years of practice as a registered nurse Preferred: A Master's Degree in Nursing Additional Information: Christian Brothers University is a Catholic university in the student-centered tradition of the De La Salle Christian Brothers. CBU fosters academic excellence in a range of programs to prepare students from all faiths and backgrounds for careers and lives informed by the Lasallian values of faith, service, and community. Christian Brothers University offers equal employment opportunity to all applicants for employment, regardless of sex, age, race, color, religion, sexual orientation, national and ethnic origin or disability. Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must apply and upload the following documents: Cover letter Résumé or CV Diversity statement Salary history/requirements Candidates who do not submit these documents will not be considered for the position. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Christian Brothers University 650 East Parkway South, Memphis Tennessee 38104"
    },
    "https://cbu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=188490": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Christian Brothers University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Nursing Christian Brothers University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Nursing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Nursing Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Memphis, TN Posted: May 27, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position ID: 188490 Share About Christian Brothers University: CBU is committed to creating and maintaining a rigorous and enriching learning experience for our students by providing them the best instruction and support by a superior faculty and staff. CBU encourages opportunities to celebrate diversity in an environment that prepares our students to be global citizens. CBU is an attractive and safe campus environment, and it is quite possibly one of the friendliest campuses anywhere. If you would like to contribute to these hallmarks of a CBU education, please consider applying for our faculty or staff vacancies through these current employment opportunities. Job Description: The Nursing Program seeks a passionate, experienced faculty member to join our undergraduate nursing program. The ideal candidate will facilitate learning in the didactic, lab, or clinical setting. Candidates will demonstrate excellence in teaching through innovative, evidence-based practice. This role is a wonderful opportunity for a dedicated nurse educator to shape the future of the nursing workforce with compassionate, skilled, and knowledgeable nursing professionals. Key Responsibilities: Facilitate learning (Didactic, lab, or clinical) Facilitate learner development and socialization Utilize assessment and evaluation strategies Participate in curriculum design and evaluation of program outcomes Function as a change agent and leader Pursue continuous quality improvement in the nurse educator role Engage in scholarship Advising and student support Actively function within the educational environment. Institutional engagement and advancement Exhibit Lasallian principles in the academic environment Requirements: A doctoral degree (Ph.D., DNP, DNSc) is preferred. (Note: To be considered for the appointment of Assistant Professor, the candidate must have a doctoral degree by the time of initial appointment. Otherwise, candidates will be considered for an Instructor position). Credentialed to teach Nursing at the University level. At a minimum, this usually requires an MSN degree from an accredited college/university. Consideration will be given to those candidates with an MSN in Nursing Education. Current or eligible for an active, unencumbered Tennessee registered nursing license or multistate licensure privilege to practice as a registered nurse in Tennessee. Strong interpersonal communication and organizational skills. Additional Information: Christian Brothers University is a Catholic university in the student-centered tradition of the De La Salle Christian Brothers. CBU fosters academic excellence in a range of programs to prepare students from all faiths and backgrounds for careers and lives informed by the Lasallian values of faith, service, and community. Christian Brothers University offers a comprehensive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability insurance, flexible spending, retirement pension plan, 403(b), and both undergraduate and graduate tuition waiver plans. CBU also offers tuition waivers for dependents of employees and participates in the Tuition Exchange Program, a reciprocal scholarship exchange program for family members of full-time faculty and staff. Christian Brothers University offers equal employment opportunity to all applicants for employment, regardless of sex, age, race, color, religion, sexual orientation, national and ethnic origin or disability. Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must apply and upload the following documents: Cover letter Résumé or CV Diversity Statement Evidence of teaching effectiveness Statement of teaching philosophy Salary history/requirements Candidates who do not submit these documents will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Christian Brothers University 650 East Parkway South, Memphis Tennessee 38104"
    },
